  "question": {
    "text": "A body of mass <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>m</mi></math> moving with velocity <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>v</mi></math> collides head-on elastically with another body of mass <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mi>m</mi></math> which is initially at rest. The ratio of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>K</mi><mo>.</mo><mi>E</mi><mo>.</mo></math> of mass <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>m</mi></math> before and after the collision will be",
